.TH DSTP 1 "August 2026" "dstp" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dstp \- run networking diagnostics against a host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dstp
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIHOST\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
dstp runs parallel checks (ping, DNS, TCP/UDP, TLS, HTTP/HTTPS, and optionally traceroute/whois/MTU) and prints a summary. Exit status is 1 if any executed check fails.
.SH OPTIONS
See
.B dstp --help
for the full flag list.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/dstp/config.yaml
Optional defaults (out, timeout, dns, skip, etc.). CLI flags override the file.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
dstp example.com
.TP
dstp example.com -o json --skip ping
.TP
dstp example.com --extra -q
.SH SEE ALSO
ping(8), traceroute(8), whois(1)
